# ============================================================
#  Endings. `kind: early` endings are only reached via `end <id>`
#  and stay exclusive (game over).
#  Graduation builds a yearbook (design §10.5) from `slot:`s, each
#  checked in descending `priority`:
#    headline (default)  1: the career you signed on the last day
#                           (`took_<career>`, last_career); none
#                           signed: still looking or back home;
#                           `ending_graduate` (no `when`) is the
#                           fallback
#    mystery             0-1: the Hollow Star outcome
#    relationships       0-3: bonds kept on the last day
#    personal            0-2: academic standing, and the lines you
#                           let the yearbook keep (last_remembered)
#  Every line is told, and chosen where there is a choice, by a
#  card on the last day (last_day.grim, feedback 2026-10-25).
#  `excludes:` drops other endings once this one is picked.
# ============================================================

# ---------------- Early endings ----------------

@ending ending_sent_home
kind: early
title: Sent Home
art: cross
text: The infirmary writes to your family. A carriage comes for you on a grey morning and you watch the towers shrink in the rear window. Your body gave out before your dreams did. Perhaps, one day, you will come back.

@ending ending_quiet_departure
kind: early
title: The Quiet Departure
art: rain
text: You take the dawn barge without telling anyone. The academy does not notice right away; then, one by one, people do. Some of them write. You keep the letters in a box you don't open for years. When you finally do, you are someone gentler, and you find you are not alone.

@ending ending_expelled
kind: early
title: Expelled
art: scales
text: The Board's decision is final. Your wand is not taken — Lumenhold is not cruel — but your name is struck from the register in ink that cannot be unwritten. You walk out of the gates with a trunk and a lesson, and the long road ahead is entirely your own.

@ending ending_hollow_claimed
kind: early
title: Claimed by the Hollow Star
art: moon
text: You open the door beneath the lake. The Hollow Star looks back. For a moment you understand everything, and then there is no "you" left to understand it. On clear nights students swear they see a new star, black against black, right above the seventh tower.

@ending ending_runaway
kind: early
title: Gone With the Wind
art: map
text: You and Corvin leave Lumenhold on a stolen sky-barge at midnight, laughing so hard you can barely steer. The academy will tell the story for years — usually wrong. You never graduate. You don't regret it, mostly.

# ---------------- Final endings (graduation) ----------------

@ending ending_hollow_keeper
slot: mystery
priority: 100
title: Keeper of the Hollow Star
art: moon
when: flag(hollow_bargain)
text: You graduate with a black star on your palm and a voice in the back of your mind that is not entirely yours. The Hollow Star gave you power; it will want something back. For now, the towers bow a little when you pass, and even the headmistress looks away first.

@ending ending_hollow_freed
slot: mystery
priority: 98
title: Herald of the Hollow Star
art: moon
when: flag(hollow_freed)
text: The spring the lake froze, the Star went free, and you held the door. It did not swallow you; it remembered who let it out. The Northern families write to you as one of their own now, and wherever you walk, candles burn a little lower, as if bowing. Lumenhold still hands you a diploma. Nobody at the ceremony looks you in the eye.

@ending ending_hollow_failed
slot: mystery
priority: 90
title: The Night Was Lost
art: door
when: flag(hollow_failed)
text: The spring the lake froze, you went down beneath it, and the door would not close for you. The headmistress closed it in your place and paid for it with years she didn't have to spare. The Wardens don't blame you. Every spring, when the lake thaws, you do, a little, and then you get up and keep the old doors anyway.

@ending ending_hollow_hero
slot: mystery
priority: 95
title: Warden of Lumenhold
art: shield
when: flag(hollow_sealed)
text: The academy will never fully know what you did beneath the lake. The headmistress does. At graduation she gives you a silver key without a lock and a seat among the Wardens, the quiet few who keep the old doors closed. Kael stands in the crowd and, for once, he is smiling.

@ending ending_archmage
priority: 80
title: The Archmage's Path
art: wand
when: flag(took_conclave)
text: In the autumn you climb the steps of the Seven Towers in a new grey robe, an apprentice of the Conclave, with seven years of wards and failures ahead and a desk that faces a wall of locked books. Professor Thorne shakes your hand at the gate and says, gruffly, "Don't waste it." You won't.

@ending ending_scholar
priority: 75
title: Scholar of the Spire
art: book
when: flag(took_fellowship)
text: Your thesis is shelved in the Spire Library, in the section students whisper about, and you take the junior fellowship that came with it. You will spend your life among books that bite and secrets that wait — and you could not be happier.

@ending ending_beloved
slot: relationships
priority: 70
title: Hand in Hand
art: heart
when: bonds(partner) > 0
text: Graduation is a blur of robes and cheers, but what you remember is a hand finding yours as the hats go up. Whatever comes next, you won't face it alone. Lumenhold taught you magic; it also taught you this.

# A partner ending names them (playtest 2, B31); each replaces the generic one above.

@ending ending_beloved_lyra
slot: relationships
priority: 72
title: The Second Flame
art: heart
when: bond(lyra) == "partner"
excludes: ending_beloved
text: When the hats go up, {lyra} catches yours before it lands and hands it back without a word. Later, in front of her whole family, she takes your hand and doesn't let go. For House Vaneshade, that is a declaration. For her it is simpler: she has finally found someone she doesn't need to beat.

@ending ending_beloved_tobias
slot: relationships
priority: 72
title: Home, Wherever
art: heart
when: bond(tobias) == "partner"
excludes: ending_beloved
text: {tobias} cries through the whole ceremony and blames the pollen. Afterwards he lifts you off your feet in front of everyone, then shows you a drawing of a farmhouse with two chairs on the porch. "No pressure," he says. "The goats have already voted."

@ending ending_beloved_seraphine
slot: relationships
priority: 72
title: Already Foreseen
art: heart
when: bond(seraphine) == "partner"
excludes: ending_beloved
text: "I saw this," {seraphine} says as the hats go up. "Years ago. You were holding my hand." You are. For once she smiles at the present, as if it has finally caught up with her, and asks whether you'd like to know what happens next. You tell her you'd rather find out together.

@ending ending_beloved_corvin
slot: relationships
priority: 72
title: No More Jokes
art: heart
when: bond(corvin) == "partner"
excludes: ending_beloved
text: {corvin} slips a key into your palm during the speeches. It opens nothing at Lumenhold; he has checked. "It's for wherever we end up," he says, and for once he doesn't make a joke of it. Then he does, of course. But his hand stays in yours.

@ending ending_beloved_mir
slot: relationships
priority: 72
title: Built to Last
art: heart
when: bond(mir) == "partner"
excludes: ending_beloved
text: {mir} has rigged the hats to fly back down. Most of them do. In the cheerful chaos they press a small brass ring into your hand; it ticks faintly, like a second heart. "It'll run for fifty years," they say. "Probably. We should check."

@ending ending_beloved_kael
slot: relationships
priority: 72
title: Thaw
art: heart
when: bond(kael) == "partner"
excludes: ending_beloved
text: {kael} doesn't throw his hat. He stands beside you in the crowd, and when the cheering is loudest he says, very quietly, "Come north with me. Or I stay. Either." It is the longest sentence about feelings he has ever spoken. His hand, in yours, is warm.

@ending ending_beloved_nessa
slot: relationships
priority: 72
title: Front Page
art: heart
when: bond(nessa) == "partner"
excludes: ending_beloved
text: The Ledger's graduation issue runs a small notice at the bottom of page six, set in {nessa}'s own type: two names, one line, no comment. All of Lumenhold reads it before breakfast. {nessa} pretends not to watch them read it, and holds your hand under the table the whole time.

@ending ending_alchemist
priority: 65
title: Master of the Crucible
art: cauldron
when: flag(took_shop)
text: Your potions are already sold under the counter in three cities. On graduation day you sign the lease on the crooked little shop by the harbour. The sign reads your name, and underneath: NO REFUNDS FOR TRANSFORMATIONS.

@ending ending_celebrity
slot: personal
priority: 60
title: The Name on Every Lip
art: star
when: renown >= 45 and flag(remember_renown)
text: The Lumen Ledger runs a special edition about you. First-years queue for your autograph. You graduate as the most talked-about student in a generation, and the world beyond the gates is already waiting to hear what you'll do next.

@ending ending_merchant
priority: 55
title: Gold in the Vaults
art: coin
when: flag(took_trading)
text: You leave Lumenhold with a diploma, a fortune and an old partner's desk in a harbour shipping house. Magic, you've decided, is good, but compound interest is better. Within five years the house has offices in every port — and an enchanted ledger that never loses a coin.

@ending ending_shadow
priority: 50
title: The Quiet Hand
art: mask
when: flag(took_unseen)
text: No one quite knows how you graduated with those grades. No one quite remembers the favours you called in. In the autumn you take a desk at the Crown's Office of Unseen Affairs, in a building with no sign and no address. You'd found it, of course, long before they told you where it was.

@ending ending_beloved_friends
slot: relationships
priority: 45
title: The Ones Who Stayed
art: group
when: bonds(friend) + bonds(close) >= 3 and flag(kept_friends)
text: You may not leave as the brightest or the richest, but you leave surrounded. Your friends throw their hats higher than anyone's, and the photograph from that day — all of you squinting into the sun — will hang in every home you ever have.

@ending ending_barely
slot: personal
priority: 65
title: By the Skin of Your Teeth
art: hourglass
when: (turn > 4 and gpa < 2.0) or flag(thesis_resubmit)
text: Your name is called last, after a long pause and some whispering between examiners. But it is called. You graduate. You are a mage of Lumenhold, and nobody ever has to know the details.

@ending ending_bystander
slot: mystery
priority: 20
title: Someone Else's Lantern
art: lantern
when: not (flag(hollow_sealed) or flag(hollow_bargain) or flag(hollow_freed) or flag(hollow_failed) or flag(hollow_fled) or flag(hollow_held_line))
text: There was a spring frost, the year you graduated, and a night when the bell under the lake would not stop ringing. You were somewhere else: asleep, or studying, or holding a door shut for the first-years. Someone else went down with the lantern. You never learn their whole story, but every spring, when the lake thaws, you find yourself grateful to them.

@ending ending_graduate
priority: 0
title: A Mage of Lumenhold
art: tower
text: Robes, hats, a speech that runs long. You walk out of the gates of Lumenhold a qualified mage — not legendary, not disgraced, simply yourself, with four years of stories and a whole world to spend them in.

@ending ending_teacher
priority: 72
title: The Teacher's Desk
art: feather
when: flag(took_teaching)
text: In the autumn you return to Lumenhold — not on the student barge, but on the faculty one. Your classroom has a window over the lake and a desk with somebody else's initials carved in it. On the first day a terrified first-year asks a question you once asked. You know exactly what to say.

@ending ending_wanderer
priority: 58
title: The Road of Wonders
art: tent
when: flag(took_circus)
text: You join the Travelling Circus of Wonders as its youngest illusionist. For years you cross the kingdoms in a painted wagon, making dragons out of moonlight for children who have never seen magic. Every winter, a letter arrives from Lumenhold. You always write back.

# ---------------- Relationship lines: Ilse Dumont's chain ----------------

@ending ending_tamsin_friends
slot: relationships
priority: 40
title: A Friend Across the Hills
art: letter
when: flag(tamsin_friends) and rel(tamsin) >= 15 and flag(kept_tamsin)
text: Your yearbook entry has a green seal pressed into the corner, which is not allowed. Tamsin Reed of Thornwick sent it, with a note: "Four years of rivalry, four hundred letters, one friend. Insufferable to the end." Every spring, at a town halfway between, there are biscuits.

@ending ending_dumonts_reunited
slot: relationships
priority: 50
title: Two Dumonts in the Photograph
art: snow
when: flag(dumont_reunited) and flag(kept_dumonts)
text: In the graduation photograph, at the edge of the crowd, two pale heads lean together: Kael, and the sister who was raised to open the door he refused. Neither of them is smiling at the camera. They are smiling at each other, which is rarer, and which you helped to happen.

@ending ending_ilse_taken
slot: relationships
priority: 45
title: A Chair Left Empty
art: rain
when: flag(ilse_taken) and not flag(dumont_reunited) and flag(kept_ilse_chair)
text: The man in grey took Ilse north, and no letter has come. At graduation Kael keeps the seat beside him empty without saying why. You know why. Some evenings, when the lake goes very still, you still look for a girl in white furs on the far shore.

# ---------------- Personal lines (yearbook) ----------------

@ending ending_thesis_hollowstar
slot: personal
priority: 35
title: The Thesis They Locked Away
art: book
when: flag(thesis_hollowstar) and flag(remember_thesis)
text: Your thesis on the founders' seal earned a distinction and then disappeared into the headmistress's tower. Its catalogue card in the Spire Library reads only "Restricted", in her handwriting. Three people in the world have read it. One of them still writes to you with questions.

@ending ending_lumen
slot: personal
priority: 30
title: A Lantern for Others
art: lantern
when: alignment >= 60 and flag(remember_lumen)
text: In the yearbook, under your portrait, someone has written: "The one you went to when it mattered." First-years you barely remember will name their own lanterns after you. Lumenhold has a word for people like that. It is the same word as its name.

@ending ending_hollow_touched
slot: personal
priority: 30
title: The Shadow at Your Heel
art: mask
when: alignment <= -60 and flag(remember_hollow)
text: Your portrait in the yearbook is the only one where the candles behind you seem to have gone out. People step aside when you pass, not quite knowing why. The Hollow has learned your name, and you find, more and more often, that you answer to it.

# ---------------- The Night's other outcomes (mystery; feedback 2026-10-25) ----------------

@ending ending_hollow_fled
slot: mystery
priority: 85
title: The Door Left Ajar
art: door
when: flag(hollow_fled)
text: You went down beneath the frozen lake, saw the door, and ran. Nobody blames you to your face; the headmistress, whose hair went white that night, never mentions it at all. Somewhere under the water the door still stands ajar. Every spring, when the ice goes out, you dream of the dark between the gap and the frame.

@ending ending_held_the_line
slot: mystery
priority: 80
title: The Night Above the Ice
art: shield
when: flag(hollow_held_line)
text: The night the lake froze, you didn't go down. You held the doors of the first-year tower against frost and whispers until dawn, and every child in it lived. Someone else went beneath the lake, or no one did; the first-years never cared which. They carved your initials over that door, and nobody has dared paint them out.

# ---------------- Careers you signed on the last day (headline; feedback 2026-10-25) ----------------

@ending ending_royal_archivist
priority: 70
title: Keeper of the Folios
art: book
when: flag(took_royal_library)
text: You take the cold room at the Royal Library Archives, the one with the folios that object to being opened. Within a year you have catalogued a shelf nobody had dared touch in a century, and the keeper has stopped checking your gloves. On the staff list, under "Cataloguer", your name is in copperplate.

@ending ending_guild
priority: 64
title: A Bench at the Works
art: cauldron
when: flag(took_guild)
text: You join the Guild of Alchemists' great works as its newest journeyman, in protective clothing you paid for yourself. There are two explosions a month and none of them yours. By the second winter the foreman sends the hardest batches to your bench, and pretends he doesn't.

@ending ending_observatory
priority: 63
title: Charting the Night
art: star
when: flag(took_observatory)
text: You go back up to the plateau with the Observatory Expedition, salaried now, frostbite remedies in your pack. The nights are long and very cold and you stay awake through every one of them. Two years on, a star on the new charts carries your initials, in very small letters.

@ending ending_field_station
priority: 62
title: Out on the Moors
art: paw
when: flag(took_field_station)
text: You take the keeper's cottage at the Beastcraft Field Station: a lamp, a kettle, and more creatures than any sane person would count. The winters are long, wet and lonely. You count the creatures anyway, every one, and the foal from your summer grows up following you about like a dog.

@ending ending_thornwick
priority: 61
title: Across the Hills
art: mirror
when: flag(took_thornwick)
text: You cross the hills to Thornwick's illusion laboratory, where they think glamour is a science and are mostly right. Lumenhold says something cutting about it, as predicted. Within three years it offers to hire you back at twice the salary, as predicted. You haven't answered yet.

@ending ending_librarian
priority: 57
title: The Stacks Kept You
art: book
when: flag(took_spire)
text: You never quite leave. In the autumn you are back behind the Spire Library's reference desk, a keeper of the stacks now, with a longer ladder and a key to the shelves nobody else may reach. Footnote has not bitten you in months. Students ask you for books, and you find them every time.

@ending ending_newt
priority: 54
title: Behind the Bar
art: cup
when: flag(took_newt)
text: You stay on at the Gilded Newt, full time, behind the bar and then in charge of it. You remember who ordered the spiced cider, and who's owed a favour, and which of the card games upstairs to look away from. Students who were first-years when you graduated come in to tell you their troubles. You pour, and listen.

@ending ending_pell
priority: 53
title: Counting Drops
art: cauldron
when: flag(took_pell)
text: You stay on at Pell & Daughters, at the counter by day and among the thousand drawers by night, counting drops while Old Pell counts aloud behind you. In ten years, if you're still careful, they'll show you the drawers that never open. You are still careful.

@ending ending_courier
priority: 52
title: Over the Lake in All Weathers
art: broom
when: flag(took_courier)
text: You keep the satchel with your name on the flap and fly the lake in all weathers, letters and parcels and the occasional live delivery. The broom still pulls left. You don't. On winter nights the first-years watch your lamp crossing the ice and make wishes on it, as if you were a star.

@ending ending_clerk
priority: 45
title: A Desk and a Stamp
art: scroll
when: flag(took_clerk)
text: You take the clerk's desk from the registrar's list: stamps, ledgers and a window that looks at a wall. It isn't a dream. It pays the rent, and in the evenings you are free, and one day, quietly, you notice that the wall has a crack in it shaped exactly like a door.

@ending ending_still_searching
priority: 10
title: Still Looking
art: map
when: flag(took_none) and (gpa >= 2.5 or renown >= 30)
text: You graduate without a post, and on purpose, or near enough. Your grades will open doors and your name has been heard; the world, you've decided, can make you a better offer in its own time. You spend the autumn writing letters from a rented room above a bakery. Some of them get answers.

@ending ending_back_home
priority: 9
title: Back in Your Old Room
art: rain
when: flag(took_none) and not (gpa >= 2.5 or renown >= 30)
text: You go home with a diploma and no letter. Your old room is smaller than you remember, and the bed is too short, and for a while you lie in it until noon and let the days rot quietly by. Then, one morning, you sit up, and write to the registrar about her list. It was still there, as she said it would be.
